Subject: [PATCH] processing: name the processing thread

The capture and playback threads are named ("FileCapture", "AlsaPlayback",
"AlsaPlaybackInner"), the processing thread is not: it shares the comm
"camilladsp" with the main, signal and websocket threads. Sweetspot pins
only the audio threads to its isolated core with real-time priority and
keeps the others on the system cores: with a name it can tell them apart.

Source: HEnquist/camilladsp v4.1.3
Upstream: Not submitted (local change)

--- a/src/processing.rs
+++ b/src/processing.rs
@@ -32,7 +32,13 @@
     rx_pipeconf: crossbeam_channel::Receiver<(config::ConfigChange, config::Configuration)>,
     processing_params: Arc<ProcessingParameters>,
 ) -> thread::JoinHandle<()> {
-    thread::spawn(move || {
+    // Named like the capture and playback threads ("FileCapture",
+    // "AlsaPlayback"), so that a supervisor can tell the audio threads
+    // from the websocket, signal and main threads (Sweetspot pins only
+    // the audio threads to the isolated core with real-time priority).
+    thread::Builder::new()
+        .name("Processing".to_string())
+        .spawn(move || {
         let chunksize = conf_proc.devices.chunksize;
         let samplerate = conf_proc.devices.samplerate;
         let multithreaded = conf_proc.devices.multithreaded();
@@ -187,4 +193,5 @@
             };
         }
     })
+        .expect("failed to spawn the processing thread")
 }
